{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_function_types", "label": "Function types", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A contract with a caller. Two unintuitive rules: fewer parameters are assignable where more are expected, and a function returning something is assignable where void is expected."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_contextual_typing", "label": "Contextual typing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The one place parameters infer: when the target type is known. Callbacks to typed functions need no annotations; a standalone function always does (TS7006)."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_fewer_parameters", "label": "Fewer parameters assignability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ignoring an argument is safe; demanding one the caller never sends is not. Makes arr.map(x => ...) legal without declaring index and array."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_overloads", "label": "Function overloads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Implementation signature is not callable. Only declared overloads are visible. First matching overload wins. Prefer a union or generic unless return type truly depends on arguments."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_default_optional", "label": "Default makes parameter optional", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "subject = 'none' is subject? for callers and string in the body. subject?: string is string | undefined in the body."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_function_types", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_contextual_typing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_function_types", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_fewer_parameters", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_function_types", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_overloads", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/08-function-types.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_function_types", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_08_function_types_default_optional", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "so